  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">SALAR Support to Decentralisation and Local Self-governance in Georgia - Inception phase Decentralization and local self-governance in Georgia</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">SALAR Support to Decentralisation and Local Self-governance in Georgia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">SALAR International AB (hereafter SALAR), a fully owned subsidiary of the Swedish Association of Local Authorities and Regions (hereafter SKR) contacted the Embassy of Sweden in 2020, regarding a potential Swedish support to the local governments and the decentralisation reform in Georgia. In 2022, SALAR approached the Embassy again, with a request to support a scoping mission that would be followed up by an inception phase in order to determine the ways forward and preparea  multy-year project in Georgia. 

The overall objective of the Project is:

The inception phase will determine ways forward with the aim to prepare for a multy-year project intervention in Georgia.

The specific objectives will include:

- To further define the thematic tracks of the project with a wider range of stakeholders and experts to assess the thematic areas and potential project ideas;

- To jointly with local stakeholders design and develop the theory of change and formulate the overall objectives of the project;

- To prepare the project implementation phase, build the project team and plan concrete activities;

- To establish strategic partnerships, select partners and define collaboration for anchorage and local ownership of the project results.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">SALAR International kommer att f&#xf6;rdjupa sin f&#xf6;rst&#xe5;else av Georgiens lokala styrelsesystem, dess begr&#xe4;nsningar och m&#xf6;jligheter och utifr&#xe5;n resultaten utarbeta ett f&#xf6;rslag till st&#xf6;d f&#xf6;r decentraliseringsprocessen i Georgien.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">SALAR International will deepen its understanding of Georgia&apos;s local governance system, its constrains and opportunities and based on findings prepare proposal for supporting decentralization process in Georgia.</narrative>
  </description>
